&HEAD CHID='repro', TITLE='Smokeview per-particle avatar rotation repro' /

 A minimal 20-second case: 10 x 10 x 3 m empty room, one wall on each
 side so the 3D scene is clearly visible, no fire, no smoke. The
 pyFDS-Evac exporter layers a .prt5 + .svo on top to show the per-
 particle AZIMUTH rotation issue.

&TIME T_END=20.0 /
&MESH IJK=10,10,6, XB=0,10,0,10,0,3 /

&SURF ID='WALL', RGB=200,200,200 /

 Short stub walls around the perimeter (1 m tall, 0.2 m thick) so
 the mesh has visible 3D structure without blocking the agents.
&OBST XB= 0.0, 0.2, 0.0,10.0, 0.0, 1.0, SURF_ID='WALL' /   ! west
&OBST XB= 9.8,10.0, 0.0,10.0, 0.0, 1.0, SURF_ID='WALL' /   ! east
&OBST XB= 0.0,10.0, 0.0, 0.2, 0.0, 1.0, SURF_ID='WALL' /   ! south
&OBST XB= 0.0,10.0, 9.8,10.0, 0.0, 1.0, SURF_ID='WALL' /   ! north

&DUMP DT_PART=0.5, DT_DEVC=1.0 /

&TAIL /
